      "title": "Loading Data: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Loading Data: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Readers and Writers",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Every reader is `pd.read_*` and returns a ==DataFrame==",
                "Every writer is `df.to_*` with a ==matching format==",
                "Pairs: `read_csv`/`to_csv`, `read_parquet`/`to_parquet`, `read_sql`/`to_sql`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Load Pipeline",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Source",
                    "sub": "file, URL, buffer, DB",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parser",
                    "sub": "reads the bytes",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Type inference",
                    "sub": "guesses dtypes",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "DataFrame",
                    "sub": "RangeIndex",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:CSV, JSON}: store no types, so pandas ==infers== them",
                "{green:Parquet, SQL}: carry a ==schema==, so types survive"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choose the Format",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Format",
                "Choose it for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "CSV",
                  "Interchange"
                ],
                [
                  "Parquet",
                  "Analytics"
                ],
                [
                  "JSON",
                  "APIs"
                ],
                [
                  "SQL",
                  "Live tables"
                ],
                [
                  "Excel",
                  "Business users"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Memory is set at load time",
              "text": "`dtype`, `usecols` and `chunksize` decide whether the file fits in ==RAM==. Choose them before you load."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "read_csv Options That Matter",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "read_csv Options That Matter",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Shape the Read",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Option",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`sep=';'`",
                  "semicolon files"
                ],
                [
                  "`header=None` + `names=[...]`",
                  "file has no header row"
                ],
                [
                  "`index_col`",
                  "column used as index"
                ],
                [
                  "`usecols=['a','b']`",
                  "only those columns: less memory, faster parse"
                ],
                [
                  "`nrows=1000`",
                  "peek at a huge file"
                ],
                [
                  "`skiprows=n`",
                  "skip junk lines before the header"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df = pd.read_csv(\"sales.csv\", sep=\";\",",
                "    skiprows=2, header=None,",
                "    names=[\"id\", \"day\", \"qty\"],",
                "    usecols=[\"id\", \"qty\"], nrows=1000)"
              ],
              "note": "peek: first 1000 rows, two columns"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Missing Values, Bools, Dates",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`na_values=['NA','-']` turns those strings into ==NaN==",
                "`keep_default_na=False` turns off the built-in NaN strings",
                "`true_values` / `false_values` map strings to **bool**",
                "`parse_dates=['col']` + `date_format='%Y-%m-%d'` parses at load"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Encoding and Compression",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:UnicodeDecodeError}: the file is not UTF-8, so set `encoding='latin-1'` or `'cp1252'`",
                "Compression is ==inferred== from the `.gz` / `.zip` extension"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Dates stay text",
              "text": "Without `parse_dates`, date columns load as ==str== (`object` before pandas 3)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "dtypes on Load and chunksize",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "dtypes on Load and chunksize",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Types at Load",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`dtype={'id':'int32','city':'category'}` sets types at ==parse time==",
                "Avoids slow type-inference passes",
                "Low-cardinality strings as ==category== cut memory massively",
                "Downcast to `int8`/`int32`/`float32` when the range allows"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df = pd.read_csv(f, dtype={",
                "    'id': 'int32',",
                "    'city': 'category',",
                "    'score': 'float32'})"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Option",
                "Gives",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`'Int64'`",
                  "nullable int",
                  "missing stays `<NA>`, no float64"
                ],
                [
                  "`'string'`",
                  "nullable text",
                  "missing stays `<NA>`"
                ],
                [
                  "`'boolean'`",
                  "nullable bool",
                  "missing stays `<NA>`"
                ],
                [
                  "`dtype_backend='pyarrow'`",
                  "Arrow types",
                  "all columns Arrow-backed"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Chunked Reading",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:DtypeWarning}: inference ran per chunk on a mixed column",
                "Fix: pass `dtype` explicitly or `low_memory=False`",
                "`chunksize=100_000` returns an ==iterator of DataFrames=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Read chunk",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Filter / aggregate",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Keep partial",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Combine partials",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "parts = []",
                "for chunk in pd.read_csv(f, chunksize=100_000):",
                "    parts.append(chunk.groupby('city')['n'].sum())",
                "total = pd.concat(parts).groupby(level=0).sum()"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never keep every chunk",
              "text": "Appending whole chunks to a list uses ==the same memory as a full load==. Filter or aggregate each chunk first."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Excel, JSON and Parquet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Excel, JSON and Parquet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Excel",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`.xlsx` needs ==openpyxl== installed",
                "`sheet_name=None` returns a ==dict== of all sheets",
                "`header=1` makes the second row the header"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df = pd.read_excel('q.xlsx',",
                "    sheet_name='Sales',",
                "    usecols='A:D', header=1)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. JSON",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "orient",
                "Shape"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`records`",
                  "list of row dicts"
                ],
                [
                  "`columns`",
                  "{col: {idx: val}}"
                ],
                [
                  "`index`",
                  "{idx: {col: val}}"
                ],
                [
                  "`split`",
                  "{index, columns, data}"
                ],
                [
                  "`table`",
                  "adds a **schema**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`read_json(f, orient='records', lines=True)` reads ==NDJSON==",
                "`pd.json_normalize(data)` flattens nested dicts into columns"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Parquet",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Typed, ==columnar==, snappy-compressed; keeps dtypes and datetimes",
                "`columns=` reads only those; `filters=` pushes row filters down",
                "Beats CSV on ==speed and size==",
                "Needs ==pyarrow== or fastparquet; `partition_cols` writes a folder per value"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df.to_parquet('s', partition_cols=['year'])",
                "pd.read_parquet('s', columns=['a','b'],",
                "    filters=[('year','==',2025)])"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Missing engine",
              "text": "`ImportError` on Excel or Parquet means the ==engine package== is not installed, not that pandas is broken."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "read_sql with SQLAlchemy",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "read_sql with SQLAlchemy",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Connect and Query",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`create_engine(url)` builds the ==connection==",
                "pandas needs **SQLAlchemy** for every non-sqlite database",
                "`read_sql` + `text()` + {blue:params} runs a query into a DataFrame"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "engine = create_engine('postgresql+psycopg2://user:pw@host/db')",
                "q = text('SELECT * FROM t WHERE id > :min')",
                "df = pd.read_sql(q, engine, params={'min': 10})"
              ],
              "note": "values go in params, never in the SQL string"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which Function",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Function",
                "Takes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`read_sql_query`",
                  "a SQL string"
                ],
                [
                  "`read_sql_table`",
                  "a table name"
                ],
                [
                  "`read_sql`",
                  "dispatches to either"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`index_col`, `parse_dates`, `dtype` work like `read_csv`",
                "`chunksize=n` returns an ==iterator== of DataFrames"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Write Back",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`to_sql` writes a DataFrame to a table",
                "Default `if_exists='fail'` {red:raises} if the table exists",
                "Use `'append'`, `index=False`, `method='multi'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df.to_sql('t', engine, if_exists='append',",
                "          index=False, method='multi')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Injection",
              "text": "Never f-string user input into SQL. Always pass **params**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Loading Data Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Loading Data Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Readers by Format",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Format",
                "Key options"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "CSV",
                  "`read_csv`: `sep` `usecols` `dtype` `parse_dates` `na_values` `nrows` `chunksize` `encoding`"
                ],
                [
                  "Excel",
                  "`read_excel`: `sheet_name` `usecols` `header`; needs ==openpyxl==; `sheet_name=None` gives dict"
                ],
                [
                  "JSON",
                  "`read_json`: `orient`, `lines=True`; `json_normalize` flattens nested"
                ],
                [
                  "Parquet",
                  "`read_parquet`: `columns`, `filters`; pyarrow; keeps dtypes, smallest, fastest"
                ],
                [
                  "SQL",
                  "`read_sql(text(q), engine, params=p, chunksize=n)`; `to_sql(name, engine, if_exists='append', index=False)`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Big Files",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`usecols` + `dtype` ({green:category}, {green:int32}) cut memory",
                "`chunksize` returns an iterator: ==aggregate per chunk==",
                "Repeat loads: convert to ==Parquet== once"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "tot = 0",
                "for ch in pd.read_csv(f, usecols=[\"amt\"],",
                "        dtype={\"amt\": \"float64\"}, chunksize=100_000):",
                "    tot += ch[\"amt\"].sum()"
              ],
              "note": "filter or aggregate each chunk, keep only the partial result"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Traps",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "f-string values into SQL: use `params`",
                "Appending every chunk to a list: same memory as full load",
                "`to_sql` default `if_exists='fail'` raises if table exists"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Text formats lose types",
              "text": "CSV and JSON store no types, so pandas infers them. Parquet and SQL carry a schema."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A CSV has ids 1, 2, NA. After `pd.read_csv(f)`, what dtype is `id`, and how do you keep integers?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`float64`: NaN forces a float column",
                "Use `dtype={'id':'Int64'}` (nullable)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "You wrote `chunks = [c for c in pd.read_csv(f, chunksize=n)]` then `pd.concat(chunks)`. Why still out of memory?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Every chunk is kept, so it equals a full load",
                "Filter or aggregate each chunk, then combine the partial results"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Bug: `pd.read_sql(f\"SELECT * FROM t WHERE name='{user}'\", engine)`. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "User input in the SQL string allows injection",
                "Use `text('... :name')` with `params={'name': user}`"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
